WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
A plane comes in to land.

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.760
Its wheels hang below it, ready.

3
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.060
At the moment of touchdown, puffs
of smoke burst from the wheels.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.890
A moment later, the same wheels
roll along the same runway,

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.500
and the smoke has gone.

6
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.000
Same plane, same wheels, same runway.

7
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:22.110
So why the smoke at touchdown, and
not once the wheels are rolling?

8
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.420
In this mission, you'll find the
work a torque does as a wheel turns:

9
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.140
energy in, or energy out.

10
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.490
Then you'll read work from a
graph of torque against angle,

11
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.960
and use it to spin up a flywheel.

12
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.600
Your mission: explain why the
wheels smoke at touchdown,

13
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.280
but not once they are rolling.
